==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Delivery Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Cafeteria Cat''' at level 20 when obtained from [[Food Stall Cat Awakes!]] (may drop on the 1st stage but guaranteed on the 2nd).

==Strategy/Usage==
Food Stall Cat's low range limits his usage to short-ranged Angels such as [[Angelic Gory]], [[Gabriel]] and [[Boraphim]]; and at level 30, his anti-Angel DPS amounts to '''4,916''', or almost as much as the average [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare]] provided all [[Heaven's Fruit]]s are at 100%. Under rare circumstances, he can also work as a rusher against ranged enemies like [[Sunfish Jones]], pairing well with [[A Gift of Cats (Rare Cat)|A Gift of Cats]] if both are used for rushing. However, [[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]] is almost always better than this unit due to Mushroom having Area Attack, better range and [[Wave Attack|Wave]] Immunity, meaning that if you own Mushroom Cat, you may never use Food Stall Cat unless you need his speed.

==='''True Form'''===
While this unit is only fairly average, its True Form grants several significant boosts. The stat boosts turn an otherwise frail and situational attacker into a dangerous specialist that can dish out extreme damage to any Angel it gets a hit on and has a higher chance to survive a counterattack during its backswing. Its higher stats means it offsets itself from Mushroom Cat, whom Cafeteria Cat now outperforms in terms of damage and DPS, albeit it still has the disadvantages of lower range, lack of Wave Immunity and Single Attack. Higher speed allows it to support the frontline better, and the range bonus provides slightly more insurance against melee enemies, despite not providing new viable targets apart from [[Lutrinae Gokurakko]] and [[St. Dober]]. The higher damage, as mentioned earlier, allows it to tear through the aforementioned two if protected properly and especially [[Boraphim]].

If you own this unit, do '''NOT''' skip getting Mushroom Cat, as Mushroom can properly counter [[Angelic Beast Rajakong]] with its stronger stats, and Cafeteria will struggle since it cannot outrange his Omni-Strike.

Its Curse ability is fairly situational with little utility as it cannot hope to reach most relevant enemies, but does see applications against Gokurakko, [[Heavenly Herald Papuu]] and [[Great Angel Chibinel]], considering its high activation chance and uptime. Curse Immunity is more of a utility bonus, preventing the [[Relic Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Relic Doge Base]] and the like from removing its abilities when fighting Angels. Although primarily hindered by Single Attack, its sheer destructive power should not be discounted.

It also has decently okay general usage, serving as a rusher, similar to [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], although some rushers like [[Ancient Egg: N004 (Special Cat)|Supercar Cat]] and [[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Heavy Assault C.A.T.]] are much stronger in general.

